The embedded neighbourhood system consists of the sets equal to some stage of the embedded sequence. Its master neighbourhood is the master neighbourhood of U, which is nonempty and equals the embedded set of index zero. Every embedded set is contained in that master neighbourhood. If an embedded set is contained in the intersection of two embedded sets, the transferred inclusions give two inclusions of enumerated neighbourhoods, the intersection law of D supplies a witnessed intersection, and the existence of an intersection index returns that equation as an equality of embedded sets.
